=0A=0AIt's not a bug, this is meant to happen. This is a result of =0AMACHI=
NE_FEATURES_BACKFILL, which is intended to ensure that we can introduce =0A=
new items to MACHINE_FEATURES controlling existing functionality without =
=0Abreaking existing machine configurations by disabling the existing =0Afu=
nctionality because the configuration doesn't include it. (In older version=
s =0Aof busybox the hwclock feature was on by default - an hwclock item was=
 added =0Aat the MACHINE_FEATURES level to be able to control it).=0A=0ATo =
fix this, just add hwclock to MACHINE_FEATURES_BACKFILL_CONSIDERED in your =
=0Amachine configuration.=0A=0ACheers,=0APaul=0A=0A=0A-- =0A=0APaul Eggleto=
